---
import Section from '../layout/Section.astro';
import Container from '../layout/Container.astro';
import Icon from '../ui/Icon.astro';
---

<Section id="comparison" padY="lg" bg="default">
  <Container>
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-bgElev/40 p-6 sm:p-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6 sm:gap-4 items-start">
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-medium tracking-widest text-text-dim uppercase mb-2">Step-driven frameworks</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
            You wire the graph. You manage retries. You verify the output. The framework is a runner for the steps you wrote.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="sm:border-l sm:border-r sm:border-border sm:px-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-medium tracking-widest text-indigo uppercase mb-2">Converge</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text leading-relaxed">
            You describe done — outputs and shell checks. The runner closes the gap, retries with strategies, and survives crashes.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-medium tracking-widest text-text-dim uppercase mb-2">Why it matters</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Less wiring. Deterministic checks. State on disk you can <code class="font-mono text-text">cat</code>, kill, and resume.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 pt-6 border-t border-border text-center">
        <a
          href="/docs/comparisons"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-indigo hover:text-text transition-colors"
        >
          Compare to LangGraph, AutoGen, CrewAI
          <Icon name="lucide:arrow-right" size={14} />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Section>
